2186045417] [17592186551105 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186550474 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551105 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186550559 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551105 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186550682 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551105 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186550859 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551105 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186550929 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551105 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551105 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551105 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186550682 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551105 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "3f4d2d26-b1de-54c9-b0f1-b5c8e35847c3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551156 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186550472 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551156 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186550716 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551156 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186550748 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551156 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186550772 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551156 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186550913 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551156 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551156 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551156 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186550772 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551156 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "94ecf65d-6eea-53a0-9871-cc56796efb87" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551237 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186551156 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551237 #edb/ref 1069 "q-108578" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551237 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551237 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/44/448ae88055ea0da5dd44fb3db608b5ac71dbd3709c88edd41440c15124d74eae.png)\n\nWhich of the graphs above correspond to an invertible function?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551237 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0fa77d6e-f50d-59b7-b662-8c42e4bce6dc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551237 #edb/ref 1074 "A function is invertible if and only if it's a one-to-one function. To determine which of the functions are one-to-one, we use the horizontal line test.\n\n![](images/e5/e582f5233163be3a094ac575ba0cf2a37b417038be8894a12717ca31d401e4d6.png)\n\nFrom the above, we see that:\n\n- For graphs I, III, and IV, any horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line. Therefore, graphs I, III, and IV show one-to-one functions. As a result, those functions are invertible.\n\n- For graph II, some horizontal lines intersect the curve more than once. So, this is not a one-to-one function. As a result, it is not invertible." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551253 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186551105 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551253 #edb/ref 1069 "q-36939" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551253 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551253 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/c2/c25885ba540cda475b528516df948ae3a7547c91ca78a8dcf2034284c50a4ca6.png)\n\nDetermine the largest domain on which the function $f(x)$ (shown above) is invertible." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551253 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2c532f18-d5b7-5299-a745-04db386fb5cd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551253 #edb/ref 1074 "First, notice that the domain of our function is $x\\in [-4,4].$ \n\nA function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test.\n\n- The function $f(x)$ does not pass the horizontal line test on the interval $x\\in (-1,1).$ In this case, the horizontal line $y=1$ intersects the graph at more than one point.\n\n![](images/d2/d295d104bd8340a8701327e19103bfa8fd12622f1500c405411d2afd8bd47801.png)\n\n- Among the given options, the largest domain on which the function $f(x)$ is invertible is $x\\in [-4,-1)\\cup [0,4].$ On this domain, a horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](images/a7/a74a9a3f1fe52a7c841c763ccffb51faa922fdaec56825ef1000b5becc3534fe.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $x\\in [-4,-1)\\cup [0,4].$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
